To enable OpenTelemetry tracing for all AI SDK calls in version 7:

1. Install the `@ai-sdk/otel` package:
```bash
pnpm install @ai-sdk/otel
```

2. Register the OpenTelemetry integration once at application startup:

**For Next.js** (in `instrumentation.ts`):
```ts
import { registerOTel } from '@vercel/otel';
import { registerTelemetry } from 'ai';
import { OpenTelemetry } from '@ai-sdk/otel';

export function register() {
  registerOTel({ serviceName: 'my-ai-app' });
  registerTelemetry(new OpenTelemetry());
}
```

**For Node.js** (in your entry file):
```ts
import { registerTelemetry } from 'ai';
import { OpenTelemetry } from '@ai-sdk/otel';

registerTelemetry(new OpenTelemetry());
```

Once registered, OpenTelemetry tracing will be enabled by default for all AI SDK calls (including `generateText`, `streamText`, `embed`, etc.) without needing to add any per-call configuration [1][2].

To read how many input tokens were served from the prompt cache, use the `cacheReadTokens` property in the `inputTokenDetails` object of the `usage` object.

**Example:**
```ts
import { generateText } from 'ai';

const { usage } = await generateText({
  model: yourModel,
  prompt: '...',
});

const cachedInputTokens = usage.inputTokenDetails?.cacheReadTokens;
console.log('Cached input tokens:', cachedInputTokens);
```

The cached input tokens are available in:
- `generateText` via `result.usage.inputTokenDetails.cacheReadTokens` [1,4,5]
- `streamText` via `result.usage.inputTokenDetails.cacheReadTokens` [2]

To create an OpenAI embedding model and embed a single string, use the `embed` function with either a string model reference or a programmatic model:

```ts
import { embed } from 'ai';

const { embedding } = await embed({
  model: 'openai/text-embedding-3-small',
  value: 'sunny day at the beach',
});
```

Or programmatically:

```ts
import { openai } from '@ai-sdk/openai';
import { embed } from 'ai';

const model = openai.embedding('text-embedding-3-small');
const { embedding } = await embed({ model, value: 'sunny day at the beach' });
```

